---
import TreatmentPage from "../../../components/TreatmentPage.astro";

const T = "/services/fertility-treatment";

const page = {
  slug: "iui",
  name: "IUI Treatment",
  title: "IUI Treatment in Lahore | Procedure & Success Rate",
  description:
    "IUI treatment in Lahore: how intrauterine insemination works, who it suits, the step-by-step procedure, success factors, risks and cost with Dr. Kamran Saleem.",
  eyebrow: "IUI Treatment",
  h1: "IUI Treatment in Lahore",
  waText: "Hello, I would like to book an IUI consultation with Dr. Kamran Saleem.",
  ctaLabel: "Book an IUI consultation",
  heroSub: [
    "Intrauterine insemination (IUI) is a simple fertility treatment in which prepared sperm is placed directly into the uterus around the time of ovulation.",
    "At Kamran Fertility Clinic, Dr. Kamran Saleem offers IUI to couples in Lahore when tests show it has a realistic chance of working, and explains plainly when it does not.",
  ].join(" "),
  leadIn: [
    { rich: ["IUI works only when certain conditions are met, so a proper ", ["fertility assessment", "/services/assessment"], " comes first."] },
  ],
  sections: [
    {
      id: "what-is-iui",
      title: "What Is IUI (Intrauterine Insemination)?",
      intro: "IUI gives sperm a shorter journey. Fertilization still happens inside the body.",
      icon: "flask",
      body: [
        "In IUI, a semen sample is washed and concentrated in the laboratory so that the most active sperm are separated from the rest of the fluid. A thin, soft catheter then places these sperm into the uterus, close to the fallopian tubes, at the time an egg is released.",
        { rich: ["Because fertilization takes place naturally, IUI is less invasive and less costly than ", ["IVF", `${T}/ivf`], ". It is also less powerful, which is why selecting the right patients matters."] },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "who-is-iui-suitable-for",
      title: "Who Is IUI Suitable For?",
      intro: "IUI can help when the basic ingredients for natural conception are present but something is slightly out of sync.",
      icon: "user",
      body: [
        "IUI may be considered for:",
        { ul: [
          "Mild male-factor infertility, such as slightly reduced count or motility",
          "Ovulation problems, once ovulation has been restored with medication",
          "Unexplained infertility, in selected cases",
          "Cervical mucus problems or ejaculatory and sexual difficulties",
          "Use of donor or frozen sperm, where appropriate",
        ] },
        "IUI is generally not suitable when both tubes are blocked, when sperm quality is severely reduced, when there is advanced endometriosis, or when a woman's age or ovarian reserve makes time the main issue. In those cases, going straight to IVF or ICSI is more sensible than repeating cycles that are unlikely to work.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "tests-before-iui",
      title: "Tests You Need Before IUI",
      intro: "A few checks prevent wasted cycles.",
      icon: "document",
      body: [
        { ul: [
          "Semen analysis, to confirm there will be enough motile sperm after preparation",
          "A tubal check, such as HSG or sonohysterogram, to confirm at least one tube is open",
          "Evidence of ovulation, with hormone tests and ultrasound as needed",
          "Thyroid and prolactin levels, where cycles are irregular",
        ] },
        { rich: ["If you already have these reports, bring them. If not, our ", ["Assessment & Diagnosis", "/services/assessment"], " service covers them."] },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "iui-procedure-step-by-step",
      title: "The IUI Procedure, Step by Step",
      intro: "Each IUI cycle takes about two weeks, and the insemination itself takes only minutes.",
      icon: "calendar",
      body: [
        { h3: "1. Cycle monitoring" },
        "A baseline scan early in your cycle. In a natural cycle, ovulation is tracked by ultrasound and sometimes hormone tests. In a stimulated cycle, tablets or injections encourage one to three follicles to develop.",
        { h3: "2. Trigger injection (if used)" },
        "When a follicle is mature, a trigger injection may be given to time ovulation precisely.",
        { h3: "3. Sperm preparation" },
        "On the day of insemination, a fresh semen sample is washed and concentrated in the laboratory.",
        { h3: "4. Insemination" },
        "Usually 24 to 36 hours after the trigger, prepared sperm is placed in the uterus with a catheter. It takes a few minutes, needs no anesthesia, and feels like a cervical smear. Mild cramping can occur.",
        { h3: "5. After the procedure" },
        "You can resume normal activities. Progesterone may be prescribed to support the uterine lining. A pregnancy test is done about 14 days after IUI.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "iui-medication",
      title: "IUI With Ovulation Medication",
      intro: "Mild stimulation can improve the chance of ovulation, but it needs careful monitoring.",
      icon: "bolt",
      body: [
        "Many IUI cycles use letrozole or clomiphene tablets, and some use low-dose FSH injections. The goal is a small number of mature follicles, not many.",
        "The main risk of stimulation is multiple pregnancy, which is why ultrasound monitoring is essential. If too many follicles develop, the cycle may be cancelled or converted to avoid a high-order multiple pregnancy.",
        { rich: ["For patients with irregular cycles, restoring ovulation first is a separate step; see ", ["ovulation induction and PCOS treatment", `${T}/ovulation-induction`], "."] },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "iui-success-rates",
      title: "IUI Success Rate: What to Expect",
      intro: "The chance of pregnancy per IUI cycle is modest, and it falls with age.",
      icon: "heart",
      body: [
        "IUI is usually offered for a limited number of cycles, often three to four, with a review after each. If pregnancy does not occur, repeating the same treatment indefinitely is rarely helpful.",
        "The factors that most affect results:",
        { ul: [
          "The woman's age, the strongest factor",
          "The cause of infertility",
          "Post-wash motile sperm count",
          "Whether ovulation is well timed",
          "How long you have been trying",
        ] },
        "Dr. Kamran will give you an honest estimate based on your own results, and will recommend moving to IVF or ICSI when further IUI is unlikely to be worthwhile.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "iui-risks",
      title: "IUI Risks and Side Effects",
      intro: "IUI is a low-risk procedure, but it is not risk-free.",
      icon: "shield",
      body: [
        { ul: [
          "Mild cramping or light spotting after insemination",
          "Multiple pregnancy, mainly with ovulation medication",
          "A small risk of pelvic infection",
          "Ovarian hyperstimulation, rare with mild stimulation",
          "Ectopic pregnancy, as in any pregnancy",
          "Emotional strain from waiting and repeated cycles",
        ] },
        "Contact the clinic or seek urgent care for severe pain, heavy bleeding or fever after insemination.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "iui-vs-ivf",
      title: "IUI vs IVF: How to Decide",
      intro: "They are different treatments for different problems.",
      icon: "compare",
      body: [
        { ul: [
          "IUI suits open tubes, adequate sperm and a woman whose age allows a few cycles to be tried.",
          "IVF suits blocked tubes, severe male factor, advanced age, endometriosis, or failed IUI, and allows embryo selection and freezing.",
        ] },
        { rich: ["Our guide to ", ["IVF vs IUI", "/resources/ivf-vs-iui"], " explains the decision in more detail."] },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "iui-cost-in-lahore",
      title: "IUI Cost in Lahore: What Affects the Price",
      intro: "IUI costs less than IVF, but the total depends on your plan.",
      icon: "coin",
      body: [
        "Typical cost components are:",
        { ul: [
          "Consultation and baseline tests",
          "Medication",
          "Monitoring scans",
          "Sperm preparation and insemination",
          "The number of cycles needed",
        ] },
        "Dr. Kamran will give you an itemized estimate per cycle, and a realistic view of how many cycles are worth trying.",
      ],
    },
  ],
  faqs: [
    { q: "What is IUI treatment?", a: "IUI (intrauterine insemination) is a treatment in which washed and concentrated sperm is placed directly into the uterus around ovulation, to increase the chance of natural fertilization." },
    { q: "Is IUI painful?", a: "Most women feel little more than mild cramping, similar to a cervical smear. No anesthesia is needed and the procedure takes only a few minutes." },
    { q: "What is the success rate of IUI?", a: "The chance per cycle is modest and depends mainly on age and the cause of infertility. Your doctor will give an individual estimate after your tests, rather than a general figure." },
    { q: "How many IUI cycles should we try?", a: "Usually a limited number, often three to four, reviewed after each. If pregnancy has not occurred, IVF or ICSI is usually a better next step." },
    { q: "When can I take a pregnancy test after IUI?", a: "About 14 days after the insemination. Testing sooner can be misleading, especially if a trigger injection was used." },
    { q: "Can IUI work with a low sperm count?", a: "It can with a mild reduction, if enough motile sperm remain after preparation. With a severe reduction, IVF with ICSI is more likely to work." },
    { q: "What is the difference between IUI and IVF?", a: "In IUI, sperm is placed in the uterus and fertilization occurs inside the body. In IVF, eggs are collected and fertilized in a laboratory, and an embryo is transferred." },
    { q: "Do I need bed rest after IUI?", a: "No. Most clinics suggest resting for a short while afterwards, then resuming normal activity. Strict bed rest has not been shown to help." },
  ],
  closingHeading: "IUI Treatment in Lahore With Dr. Kamran Saleem",
  closingParas: [
    "At Kamran Fertility Clinic, Dr. Kamran Saleem provides IUI for couples in Lahore, with ovulation monitoring, sperm assessment and a clear limit on how many cycles are worth trying.",
    "We recommend IUI only where tests suggest it has a realistic chance, and say so honestly when IVF or ICSI is the better route.",
  ],
  resources: [
    { href: "/resources/ivf-vs-iui", category: "Treatments", title: "IVF vs IUI: understanding the difference" },
    { href: "/resources/female-infertility-treatment", category: "Fertility Treatment", title: "Female Infertility Treatment: Causes, Medicines, Tests and Options" },
    { href: "/resources/male-fertility-test", category: "Male Fertility", title: "Male Fertility Test: What It Shows" },
  ],
  close: {
    heading: "Considering IUI?",
    body: "Bring your semen analysis, any HSG or tubal reports and recent cycle history to your consultation.",
    cta: "Book an IUI Consultation",
  },
};
---

<TreatmentPage {...page} />
